{% comment %}
  Step 5 of 5 — final review before booking. Shows a read-only summary of
  everything collected in the previous steps (doctor, patient, mode,
  day/time) and a payment-method choice.

  MOBILE REDESIGN per a later Figma pass (node 438:7468), same instruction
  as the previous four steps: stay with the design, ignore backend
  integration.
  - Header swapped to the shared kal-booking-flow-step-header.liquid
    snippet. Since this is the last step, its step-progress-bar shows a
    plain "Final step" instead of "Next : ..." — see that snippet's own
    comment for the step_number == step_total branch that does this.
  - Heading changed from "Confirm your slot" to "Confirm booking" to
    match the export; subtext unchanged.
  - The old .kal-doctor-summary avatar row above the details card is
    gone — the export has no separate doctor-summary card on this step,
    just the details list below, now starting with its own "Doctor" row
    (previously the doctor's name only appeared in that removed summary
    row, not in the details list itself).
  - Details list gained a "Doctor" row (first) and renamed "Patient Name"
    to "Patient" to match the export; "Fee" is gone from this list
    entirely — replaced by the new Payment Method section below (two
    cards: "Pay now" at a 10%-off price, "Pay at clinic" at full price).
    Both are static mock prices (₹450 / ₹495), same category as the
    doctor's photo/fee being placeholders elsewhere in this flow.
  - Payment Method cards are click-to-select (data-kal-payment-method,
    handled by setPaymentMethod() in kal-booking-flow.js) purely for
    visual state — no amount is actually charged differently, this is a
    mockup. "Pay now" starts selected, matching the export.
  - The old "pay at the clinic" notice banner is gone — payment method is
    now an explicit choice via the cards above, not a fixed notice.
  - Button text changed from "Confirm Booking" to "Confirm payment" to
    match the export; still carries data-kal-confirm-booking and
    data-kal-goto="booking-confirmed" exactly as before — see below for
    why those remain a to-do, not wired to the backend.

  "Confirm payment" is NOT wired to the backend (explicit instruction
  throughout this build — "dont integrate it"). data-kal-confirm-booking is
  a hook with no click handler yet; when backend integration happens, this
  is where the two-call sequence documented in
  kal-booking-flow-step-patient-details.liquid (create hold, then POST
  /api/public/appointments) should fire. It also carries
  data-kal-goto="booking-confirmed" so the button navigates to the
  post-booking success screen for demo purposes in the meantime — once a
  real click handler is added for the API calls, that handler should only
  call goToStep('booking-confirmed') after a successful booking, not
  unconditionally like the plain data-kal-goto does today.

  Single shared markup, not a __mobile + __desktop split — this step was
  already fully consolidated into the shared step shell before this pass
  (see "SHARED STEP SHELL" in kal-booking-flow.css), unlike the earlier
  steps in this redesign series that still have a separate desktop
  .kal-step-entry__info block to leave untouched. There's no such
  separate desktop content here to preserve, so — unlike those steps —
  this content change (dropping the doctor-summary row and the pay
  notice, adding the Doctor row and the Payment Method cards) affects
  both breakpoints, not mobile only. The now-dead desktop-only CSS
  overrides this left behind (the doctor-summary-card margin, the
  pay-notice display:none) are addressed in kal-booking-flow.css's own
  comment.
{% endcomment %}

<div class="kal-step-confirmation kal-step-shell">

  <div class="kal-step-entry__info kal-step-shell__info">
    <div class="kal-step-entry__info-content">
      <h2 class="kal-step-entry__heading">Confirm your slot</h2>
      <p class="kal-step-entry__body-text">Check the details before we hold it for you.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="kal-step-entry__location">
      <span class="kal-icon kal-icon--location">
        <!-- ICON: location-pin (not received yet) -->
      </span>
      <span class="kal-step-entry__location-text">
        Kerala Ayurveda Wellness Center, Indiranagar &middot; Opens 8 AM
      </span>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="kal-step-shell__panel">

    {%- render 'kal-booking-flow-step-header', back_target: 'patient-details', step_number: 5, step_total: 5 -%}

    <div class="kal-step-shell__scroll">
      <div class="kal-step-doctor-select__intro">
        <h2 class="kal-step-doctor-select__heading">Confirm booking</h2>
        <p class="kal-step-doctor-select__subtext">Check the details before we hold it for you.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="kal-confirmation-details">
        <p class="kal-confirmation-details__label">Consultation Details</p>
        <div class="kal-confirmation-details__divider"></div>
        <div class="kal-confirmation-details__rows">
          <div class="kal-confirmation-details__row">
            <span class="kal-confirmation-details__key">Doctor</span>
            <span class="kal-confirmation-details__value">Dr. Neethu Jayachandran</span>
          </div>
          <div class="kal-confirmation-details__row">
            <span class="kal-confirmation-details__key">Patient</span>
            <span class="kal-confirmation-details__value" data-kal-confirm-name>—</span>
          </div>
          <div class="kal-confirmation-details__row">
            <span class="kal-confirmation-details__key">Mode</span>
            <span class="kal-confirmation-details__value" data-kal-confirm-mode>—</span>
          </div>
          <div class="kal-confirmation-details__row">
            <span class="kal-confirmation-details__key">Date &amp; Time</span>
            <span class="kal-confirmation-details__value" data-kal-confirm-datetime>—</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      {%- comment -%}
        Payment Method — new per this Figma pass, replacing the old fixed
        "Fee" row + "pay at the clinic" notice. Click-to-select between
        the two cards is purely visual (setPaymentMethod() in
        kal-booking-flow.js just toggles kal-payment-option--selected) —
        both prices are static mockup values, nothing is actually
        charged differently. "Pay now" starts selected, matching the
        export.

        Same for both booking experiments (see kal-booking-flow.js's
        BOOKING EXPERIMENT comment) — the only difference between them is
        which step the flow opens on, not anything on this screen.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <div class="kal-payment-section">
        <p class="kal-payment-section__label">Payment Method</p>
        <div class="kal-payment-options">
          <button type="button" class="kal-payment-option kal-payment-option--selected" data-kal-payment-method="pay-now">
            <span class="kal-payment-option__badge">Save 10%</span>
            <span class="kal-payment-option__icon">
              {%- render 'kal-booking-icons', icon_name: 'payment-card' -%}
            </span>
            <span class="kal-payment-option__title">Pay now</span>
            <span class="kal-payment-option__divider" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            <span class="kal-payment-option__price">&#8377;450</span>
          </button>
          <button type="button" class="kal-payment-option" data-kal-payment-method="pay-at-clinic">
            <span class="kal-payment-option__icon kal-payment-option__icon--tint">
              {%- render 'kal-booking-icons', icon_name: 'clinic-building' -%}
            </span>
            <span class="kal-payment-option__title">Pay at clinic</span>
            <span class="kal-payment-option__divider" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            <span class="kal-payment-option__price">&#8377;495</span>
          </button>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="kal-step-shell__footer">
      <button type="button" class="kal-step-doctor-select__continue" data-kal-confirm-booking data-kal-goto="booking-confirmed">
        Confirm payment
      </button>
    </div>

  </div>

</div>
